[3] the symmetrised coordinate
    y = 4*q^2 + 16*q^4 + 48*q^6 + 128*q^8 + 312*q^10 + 704*q^12 + O(q^14)
    odd part of y (must be 0): 0
    y + 4*t8(2tau+1/2) = O(q^60)
    => y(tau) = -4*t8(2tau+1/2); y = 4q^2 + ..., canonical cusp
       parameter Q = q^2 (width 1/2), so |dy/dQ|(0) = 4 exactly.

